communications.communication:
To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Pennsylvania Right to Know Act, I hereby request digital copies of the following public records created, received, or retained by Farmington Township from January 1, 2023 through the date of this request:

1. Communications: All emails (and attachments), text messages, digital communications, electronic communications (e.g. Microsoft Teams chats, etc.) and written correspondence to, from, or between any Township Supervisor, Manager, Solicitor, Secretary or Engineer containing the terms: "Seneca", "Seneca Resources", "Seneca Resources Company", "Seneca Resources Company, LLC",  "National Fuel Gas", "National Fuel Gas Company", "NFG", "Covington", "Thornbottom", "Pauling", "Zemlak", "McGlaughlin", "EJB", "Breneman",  "Larson", "723", "185HU", "54041" or "117-22323";
2. Phone Logs: All telephone logs, call histories, or message registries documenting communications with Seneca Resources Company, LLC or parent corporations or subsidiaries (hereinafter "developer"), its landmen, or representatives;
3. Agreements: All contracts, Memorandums of Understanding (MOUs), excess maintenance agreements, and road bonding agreements between Farmington Township and the developer;
4. Financial Records: All ledgers, escrow account receipts, check registries, and financial records showing funds or in-kind contributions transferred from the developer to Farmington Township;
5. Meeting Records: All minutes, agendas, official notes, and transcripts from public meetings or executive sessions where the developer or well pad was discussed;
6. Enforcement Logs: All code enforcement, zoning, or police logs regarding vehicle movements or right-of-way boundaries on Thornbottom Road;

FORMAT: Native electronic format (PDF/Excel) sent via email or secure download link.

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request; I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not;

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

David Murray High
